Usage:
  feov-record [flags]
  feov-record [command]

Available Commands:
  carry           restate a closure from an earlier round: --id R2-3 --carried-from <round> [--as closed|...] [--superseded-by R3-1]. It makes no fresh claim, so it needs no --verified-by triple — but the record must already hold a closure of this gap, or the carry is refused.
  class           the gap-class registry: what KINDS of defect this run recognises
  close           close a gap WITH its verification: --id R2-3 --as closed|closed_with_regression|... --verified-by L1 --verified-with "git show" --verified-against "7bc501e:path" [--superseded-by R3-1] --reason "<what was verified and why it holds>". THE VERIFICATION TRIPLE IS THE POINT: this verb asserts that the repair was checked THIS ROUND, by you. For a closure the record already holds — work an earlier round did, which you are restating rather than re-attesting — use `carry`, which needs no triple because it makes no fresh claim. Re-closing carried work here double-counts the closure history
  closing         a ### RED CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  completion      Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  count-claims    count the FOOTNOTED declarative claims in blue's report (read-only)
  fetch           cached, hash-verified web read (replaces WebFetch); serves both sides the same bytes
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  help            Help about any command
  inquiry-support your per-round verdict that the REPORT still carries a line of inquiry: --id Q1 --as supported|weakened|unsupported|absent --reason "<what the report says for it, quoted>". Read the report ONCE this round and vote every line against that read
  mint            mint a board gap (id is TOOL-assigned; --key <stable-label> makes retries idempotent): --class <slug> --quote "<the exact sentence it lives at>" --problem "..."|--reason --fix "..." --check "<acceptance check red runs at re-audit>" --severity/--likelihood/--impact/--complexity <grade> [--supersedes R1-2,R1-7] [--found-by L5-F3,L6-F2]
  motion          file and rule on a motion — a grade dispute, a petition, or a ruling on a direction. One mechanism, one id.
  near-match      screen a candidate against the board before minting: --problem "<what is wrong>" [--quote "<the sentence it lives at>"] — returns the top 5 gaps (open AND closed) by lexical overlap, so a near-duplicate surfaces as a reopen (mint --supersedes <id>) rather than a fresh gap. The tool SCREENS and ranks; you decide reopen-or-new. Read-only: it records nothing.
  position        the round's ### RED section (prose via --reason)
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, no flags of its own — just your --run and --seat-id, and a value that disagrees with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
  regrade         same-id grade movement, recorded with its reason: --id R2-5 [--severity/--likelihood/--impact/--complexity <grade>] --reason "..."
  show            read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | work | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry
  spot-check      the round archive spot-check record (W1.8 duty): --ids R1-4,R2-7 --reason "<what the sample showed>" | --none --reason "<why there was nothing to sample>" when the archive was empty at round start
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: --as PASS|FAIL — checkpoints records/ to the recovery mirror

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for feov-record
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED on every call: the dispatch prompt names it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, as the dispatch prompt states it (SEAT_ID). REQUIRED on every call, and it SELECTS this surface: the verbs listed are the ones your seat may run
  -v, --version          version for feov-record

